        "level": "A2",
        "objective": "Form the comparative and superlative of adjectives using the elative root pattern 'أَفْعَل' (ʾAfʿal) + 'مِن' (min - than) and construct price/quality comparisons.",
        "presentation": {
            "explanation": "In Arabic, comparisons of superiority (*cheaper, bigger, better, more expensive*) are generated through a single morphological pattern called **اسم التفضيل** (Ism at-Tafḍīl / The Elative Pattern: **أَفْعَل** *'Af'al*):\n\n1. Deriving the 'Af'al Pattern from 3-Root Letters:\n   - **رَخِيص** (*rakhīṣ* - cheap) -> **أَرْخَص** (*'arkhaṣ* - cheaper)\n   - **غَالٍ** (*ghālin* - expensive) -> **أَغْلَى** (*'aghlā* - more expensive)\n   - **كَبِير** (*kabīr* - big) -> **أَكْبَر** (*'akbar* - bigger)\n   - **صَغِير** (*ṣaghīr* - small) -> **أَصْغَر** (*'aṣghar* - smaller)\n   - **جَيِّد / حَسَن** (*jayyid/ḥasan* - good) -> **أَفْضَل / أَحْسَن** (*'afḍal / 'aḥsan* - better)\n   - **قَدِيم** (*qadīm* - old) -> **أَقْدَم** (*'aqdam* - older)\n   - **جَمِيل** (*jamīl* - beautiful) -> **أَجْمَل** (*'ajmal* - more beautiful)\n\n2. The Comparative Formula: **Noun A + أَفْعَل + مِنْ + Noun B**:\n   - *'هَذَا القَمِيصُ **أَرْخَصُ مِنْ** ذَاك.'* (This shirt is **cheaper than** that one.)\n   - *'الحَرِيرُ **أَغْلَى مِنَ** القُطْن.'* (Silk is **more expensive than** cotton.)\n   - *'سُوقُ مَرَّاكُشَ **أَكْبَرُ مِنْ** هَذَا السُّوق.'* (The souk of Marrakech is **bigger than** this souk.)\n\n3. The Superlative Formula (The most ...):\n   - Place the *'Af'al* noun directly before a definite noun or in an iḍāfa:\n     - **أَفْضَلُ مَحَلٍّ فِي السُّوق** (*'Afḍalu maḥallin fī as-sūq*) = The best shop in the souk.\n     - **أَغْلَى فُسْتَان** (*'Aghlā fustān*) = The most expensive dress.",
            "examples": [
                {
                    "target": "هَذَا الخَاتَمُ الفِضِّيُّ أَرْخَصُ مِنَ الخَاتَمِ الذَّهَبِيّ.",
                    "reading": "Hādhā al-khātamu al-fiḍḍiyyu 'arkhaṣu mina al-khātami adh-dhahabiyy.",
                    "translation": "This silver ring is cheaper than the gold ring."
                },
                {
                    "target": "هَذِهِ العَبَاءَةُ أَجْمَلُ وَأَفْضَلُ جَوْدَةً مِنْ تِلْك.",
                    "reading": "Hādhihi al-'abā'atu 'ajmalu wa-'afḍalu jawdatan min tilk.",
                    "translation": "This abaya is more beautiful and of better quality than that one."
                },
                {
                    "target": "خَانُ الخَلِيلِي مِنْ أَقْدَمِ الأَسْوَاقِ فِي العَالَمِ العَرَبِيّ.",
                    "reading": "Khānu al-Khalīlī min 'aqdami al-'aswāqi fī al-'ālami al-'arabiyy.",
                    "translation": "Khan el-Khalili is among the oldest souks in the Arab world."
                }
            ],
            "mnemonics": [
                "Comparative Pattern = AF'AL ('akbar, 'aṣghar, 'arkhaṣ, 'aghlā)!",
                "MIN = Than ('arkhaṣ MIN = cheaper THAN)."
            ],
            "culturalNotes": [
                "The word 'Allāhu Akbar' (الله أكبر) uses this exact same elative pattern: 'Akbar' (أكبر) means 'greater / greatest' (God is Greater)."
            ]
        },
